{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-payment-methods-google-pay","reason":"Independently read the complete 113-line pinned raw and verified SHA-256, all five exact quotes, receipt/candidate/suggestion consistency, the online-payments route, and Q1/Q2. The entry preserves catalog-versus-enablement scope, regional/entity network conditions, Interac capture, DPAN/FPAN and 3DS qualifications, Level 1 decryption gate, and the JCB-list mismatch. One material exception is omitted from its otherwise detailed liability-shift summary: after saying Google Pay does not guarantee shift for Visa issued outside the EU/UK, raw line 73 describes an optional upgrade for those cards requiring additional transaction data, supported by Adyen APIs. A reader asking whether the regional limit has a conditional path could infer a categorical absence from the source entry and Q2."}
